From: nuno407 <11352538+nuno407@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:50:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 28/45] gpu: host1x: cancel the fence when an interruptible
 wait is interrupted

host1x_syncpt_wait() only cancels its fence on timeout. When
dma_fence_wait_timeout() returns -ERESTARTSYS, the fence stays queued on
the syncpoint interrupt list with its reference held, so every
interrupted wait leaks a fence until the syncpoint finally reaches the
threshold, or forever if it never does. Callers that retry on
-ERESTARTSYS (tegra-video) can exhaust memory this way. Cancel the fence
on any unsuccessful wait.
---
 drivers/gpu/host1x/syncpt.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/host1x/syncpt.c b/drivers/gpu/host1x/syncpt.c
index 807c74fc6..2cc35a7b0 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/host1x/syncpt.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/host1x/syncpt.c
@@ -242,7 +242,7 @@ int host1x_syncpt_wait(struct host1x_syncpt *sp, u32 thresh, long timeout,
 		return PTR_ERR(fence);
 
 	wait_err = dma_fence_wait_timeout(fence, true, timeout);
-	if (wait_err == 0)
+	if (wait_err <= 0)
 		host1x_fence_cancel(fence);
 	dma_fence_put(fence);
 
